<section style="padding:80px 0;">
  <div class="container" style="max-width:900px;">
    <h1 style="margin-bottom:16px;">The Science of Light Therapy</h1>
    <p style="font-size:1.2rem;color:var(--color-grey-mid);margin-bottom:64px;">Understanding the research behind our technology</p>

    <div style="margin-bottom:64px;" data-animate>
      <h2 style="margin-bottom:24px;">What Is Red Light Therapy?</h2>
      <p style="margin-bottom:16px;">Red light therapy (also called photobiomodulation or low-level laser therapy) is a non-invasive treatment that uses specific wavelengths of red and near-infrared light to stimulate cellular processes in the body. Unlike UV light which can damage skin, red and near-infrared wavelengths are safe and have been the subject of thousands of published studies.</p>
      <p>The key insight is that certain wavelengths of light — particularly 630–670nm (visible red) and 810–850nm (near-infrared) — are absorbed by chromophores in our cells, triggering a cascade of beneficial biological processes including increased ATP production, improved circulation, and reduced inflammation.</p>
    </div>

    <div style="background:var(--color-black);color:white;border-radius:24px;padding:48px;margin-bottom:64px;" data-animate>
      <h2 style="color:white;margin-bottom:32px;">How Our Wavelengths Work</h2>
      <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:32px;">
        <div style="background:rgba(200,16,46,0.2);border:1px solid rgba(200,16,46,0.4);border-radius:16px;padding:28px;">
          <div style="font-size:2rem;font-weight:700;color:#C8102E;font-family:var(--font-heading);margin-bottom:8px;">650nm</div>
          <h3 style="color:white;margin-bottom:12px;">Visible Red Light</h3>
          <p style="color:rgba(249,247,244,0.7);font-size:0.9rem;">Penetrates the outer layers of skin and scalp. Studied for stimulating hair follicles, improving skin texture, and boosting collagen production at the surface level.</p>
        </div>
        <div style="background:rgba(201,168,76,0.2);border:1px solid rgba(201,168,76,0.4);border-radius:16px;padding:28px;">
          <div style="font-size:2rem;font-weight:700;color:#C9A84C;font-family:var(--font-heading);margin-bottom:8px;">850nm</div>
          <h3 style="color:white;margin-bottom:12px;">Near-Infrared Light</h3>
          <p style="color:rgba(249,247,244,0.7);font-size:0.9rem;">Penetrates deeper into tissue. Studied for reaching the dermal papilla of hair follicles, reducing inflammation, and supporting cellular repair at a deeper level.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div style="margin-bottom:64px;" data-animate>
      <h2 style="margin-bottom:32px;">Published Research</h2>
      <p style="margin-bottom:24px;color:var(--color-grey-mid);font-size:0.9rem;font-style:italic;">The following peer-reviewed studies are referenced for educational purposes only. Lumisca devices have not been independently tested in clinical trials. Individual results may vary.</p>
      <div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:16px;">
        <div style="padding:24px;background:#f5f3f0;border-radius:12px;border-left:4px solid var(--color-red);">
          <p style="font-weight:700;margin-bottom:4px;color:var(--color-black);">Laser Phototherapy — Hair Regrowth</p>
          <p style="font-size:0.85rem;color:var(--color-grey-mid);">Avram &amp; Rogers (2009) — Lasers in Surgery and Medicine. Study examining the use of low-level laser therapy for androgenetic alopecia, noting improvements in hair count.</p>
        </div>
        <div style="padding:24px;background:#f5f3f0;border-radius:12px;border-left:4px solid var(--color-red);">
          <p style="font-weight:700;margin-bottom:4px;color:var(--color-black);">Red Light &amp; Collagen Synthesis</p>
          <p style="font-size:0.85rem;color:var(--color-grey-mid);">Barolet et al. (2009) — Journal of Investigative Dermatology. Research examining how 660nm red light may stimulate fibroblast activity and collagen production in skin tissue.</p>
        </div>
        <div style="padding:24px;background:#f5f3f0;border-radius:12px;border-left:4px solid var(--color-red);">
          <p style="font-weight:700;margin-bottom:4px;color:var(--color-black);">Photobiomodulation &amp; Cellular Energy</p>
          <p style="font-size:0.85rem;color:var(--color-grey-mid);">Hamblin (2016) — Photochemistry and Photobiology. Overview of mechanisms by which red and near-infrared light may stimulate mitochondrial cytochrome c oxidase and increase ATP production.</p>
        </div>
        <div style="padding:24px;background:#f5f3f0;border-radius:12px;border-left:4px solid var(--color-red);">
          <p style="font-weight:700;margin-bottom:4px;color:var(--color-black);">Sleep Quality &amp; Near-Infrared Light</p>
          <p style="font-size:0.85rem;color:var(--color-grey-mid);">Zhao et al. (2012) — Journal of Athletic Training. Research into the effect of near-infrared light on sleep quality and melatonin levels in participants over a 2-week period.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div style="text-align:center;background:var(--color-red);border-radius:24px;padding:48px;color:white;" data-animate>
      <h2 style="color:white;margin-bottom:16px;">Ready To Try It?</h2>
      <p style="color:rgba(255,255,255,0.85);margin-bottom:32px;">60-day money back guarantee. Free UK delivery. Results or your money back.</p>
      <a href="/collections/all" class="btn btn-ghost">Shop The Collection</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

